return [[<font size="15" color="rgb(150, 150, 150)"><b>Using the UI</b></font>

Fork3X brings a bunch of keybinds for controllers that make building faster and more intuitive, and avoid the necessity of triggering UI navigation manually.

 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">•</font> You can switch tools by pressing the <b>left and right buttons of your D-Pad</b>.
 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">•</font> Pressing the L2 button will directly select the current tool's window with UI navigation.
 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">•</font> Pressing the left thumbstick (for moving) will auto-select the bottom of the panel on the right.
 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">•</font> Drag bubbles (aka handles) can be dragged by pressing R2.
 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">•</font> The X and Y buttons (or cross and triangle on DualShock controllers) can trigger keybinds. These are explained when pressing the tool's ❔ button.

{split}

<font size="15" color="rgb(150, 150, 150)"><b>Selecting</b></font>

You can select parts in multiple ways:

 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">•</font> You can select a single part by simplying pressing R2 on the part.
 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">•</font> You can select muliple parts individually by enabling multiselection (the + button in the panel on the right).
 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">•</font> You can press the button with two squares (near the bottom of the panel) to select parts that overlap the ones you're selecting.

{split}

<font size="15" color="rgb(150, 150, 150)"><b>Grouping</b></font>

To group/ungroup part, you must use the <b>arrangement utility</b>. This must be done like this:
 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">1.</font> Select the parts you want to group, or the model you want to ungroup.
 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">2.</font> In the panel on the right, find a button whose icon is a folder.
 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">3.</font> Follow the instructions displayed to perform the desired action.

{split}

<font size="15" color="rgb(150, 150, 150)"><b>Saving your creations</b></font>

Fork3X lets users save their creations to use them in the same place, and export them for use in Studio.

 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">•</font><b>To save a build,</b> click the floppy disk icon (💾) in the panel on the right. The procedure is explained when pressing the ❔ button.
 <font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">•</font><b>To export a build (if allowed),</b> press the &lt;-[] icon in the panel on the right. Your build will be exported into a short code.
 
Install the import plugin in <b>Roblox Studio</b> to import your creation thanks to said code:
<font color="rgb(150, 150, 150)">roblox.com/library/142485815</font>

Note that Fork3X, as a different F3X version, will only get partly saved by F3X's system.

Can't export? Ask the developer if they can use the test place's version and not the free model.

{split}

